// contractus.exsc -- the interface every UTF-8 -> UTF-16 library here implements.
//
// A library is ONE file defining
//
//     publica functio converte(fons: acies<u8, 4096>, n: mensura,
//                              scopus: &mutabilis acies<u16, 4096>,
//                              modus: u8) -> Exitus
//
// and nothing else public. It is pure: no `poscit`, no allocation, no
// standard stream. It reads fons[0..n) as UTF-8 and writes UTF-16 CODE UNITS
// -- values, not bytes -- to scopus[0..unitates). Byte order is not its
// business: spec 1 says nothing may read the host's, and a library that never
// serialises cannot get it wrong. probatio.exsc serialises, little or big
// endian as its input asks.
//
// WELL-FORMED means Unicode 17 section 3.9, Table 3-7: the only second-byte
// ranges that are not 80..BF are E0 A0..BF, ED 80..9F, F0 90..BF and F4 80..8F.
// That is what refuses overlong forms, UTF-16 surrogates (U+D800..U+DFFF)
// and anything above U+10FFFF, with no check on the decoded value.
//
// TWO MODES, one function, because the two policies differ only at the
// moment a sequence is found ill-formed:
//
//   modus_stricte    stop at the first ill-formed subpart. Exitus.status is
//                    status_malformatum, Exitus.positio the byte offset of
//                    that subpart's first byte, and scopus[0..unitates) holds
//                    the conversion of everything BEFORE it -- not nothing.
//
//   modus_substitue  never fail. Each MAXIMAL SUBPART of an ill-formed
//                    subsequence (section 3.9, "U+FFFD substitution of
//                    maximal subparts"; the practice WHATWG and Python's
//                    decoder follow) becomes ONE U+FFFD, and decoding resumes
//                    at the first byte after it. status is status_bene.
//
// A maximal subpart is the longest prefix of the remaining bytes that is the
// start of some well-formed sequence. So E0 80 80 is THREE replacements (E0
// alone cannot be followed by 80), F0 90 80 at the end of input is ONE, and a
// stray 80 is one. Every library has to get exactly this right -- it is the
// part that separates a decoder that merely works on valid text from one that
// agrees with every other.
//
// CAPACITY. 4096 bytes in, 4096 units out. Output never exceeds input in
// length: a 1-, 2- or 3-byte sequence makes one unit, a 4-byte sequence two,
// and a replacement covers at least one byte and makes one. n greater than
// 4096 is the caller's error and no library is asked to survive it.

publica structura Exitus {
    unitates: mensura
    status: u8
    positio: mensura
}

publica firma modus_stricte: u8 = 0;
publica firma modus_substitue: u8 = 1;
publica firma status_bene: u8 = 0;
publica firma status_malformatum: u8 = 1;
// 2: a lockstep library's comparator found its redundant decoders disagreeing.
// A healthy library never returns it; the corpus is there to prove none does.
publica firma status_discrepantia: u8 = 2;
